Z||000000||Nyte||04-30-2001||03:33 AM||||Do it, 'cause I am thinking about doing it and I might regret it afterwards, like I hear some people say.<P>Now I drive a '92 Chevy Blazer with the 4.3 liter V6.  I'm making payments on it.  I date a lot so I drive a lot, and fuel prices are killing me!<P>I'm not ALL into racing so I don't need the power.  But I don't want to putt-putt around either.  Shoot I don't even remember how  quick my Fiero drives, I haven't driven it since December.  But I do know the Blazer has crazy torque and I love it.<P>So you guys think it'll be worth it, or no?<P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"<p>[This message has been edited by Nyte (edited 04-30-2001).]||||reg||4
