Z||000009||Nyte||04-30-2001||04:57 PM||||Check this out guys, this is what I'm going to do...<P>I'm going to go ahead and restore the Duke to save me money.  Like everyone knows, Plastic Duke or Monster 350, it's a beautiful car.  I'm going to also restore everything around it.  Interior, body panels, suspension and the like.  Down the line when I REALLY have money to burn like I do now, I'll purchase a nice V6 notchback/coupe.  I'll then restore that engine or do whatever engine swap I want to perform and <B>swap</B> all my exterior and interior mods I did to the '84 onto the new car.<P>You see, I don't want to go out and pay two thousand for a smaller fuel efficent decent car when I can spend eight hundred to a thousand to fix the car I already have.  I mean, back when I did drive it, the dang thing has no left fender and everyone STILL loved it's looks.  <I>Everyone</I>.<P>Sound like a plan?<P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"<p>[This message has been edited by Nyte (edited 04-30-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000010||JohnnyK||04-30-2001||05:14 PM||||I guess that depends on what you mean by "everyone still jocked". If you mean laugh, of course they're going to laugh if your driving around without a fender on a Fiero..||||reg||1
Z||000011||RedOktober||05-01-2001||04:18 AM||||DO IT... But do it right. <P>My Duke was bought for $250 ..3 years ago. since then I 've only put in a clutch, struts, and brakes. It gets an oil change every 5000k's and will start up everytime...even if I haven't driven it in months. <P>It is a great little car, lighter than my GT or SE and is alot more fun on the twisties. BTW it gets better gas milage( which is always a good thing). <P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
